# Assets and Images Conventions

Everything static lives under `assets/`. Brand files are referenced from
config. `assets/icons/` holds stroke-rounded Hugeicons SVGs copied from
`@hugeicons-pro/core-stroke-rounded`, the same set diamond-app renders.
`assets/images/` holds article screenshots referenced from MDX.

## Structure

```text
assets/
├── favicon.svg
├── logo/
│   ├── light.svg          # used on dark backgrounds (branding.json logo.dark)
│   └── dark.svg           # used on light backgrounds (branding.json logo.light)
├── icons/
│   └── <hugeicon-name>.svg    # album-01.svg is Album01Icon, the Projects sidebar icon
└── images/
    └── <tab>/<section>/<article>-<task>-<n>.webp
        # assets/images/guides/projects/overview-create-1.webp
        # assets/images/guides/projects/overview-create-1-dark.webp
```

## Patterns

- Brand files are SVG and are referenced only from `docs.json` and
  `config/branding.json` with root paths (`/assets/logo/dark.svg`).
- Icon files use a `0 0 24 24` viewBox and `stroke="oklch(0.552 0.016 285.938)"`,
  the app's `muted-foreground` (zinc-500), the same in light and dark. Do not
  use `currentColor`: Mintlify loads these files as images, so it would render
  black. The file name is the Hugeicons export in kebab-case without the
  `Icon` suffix (`Album01Icon` → `album-01.svg`).
  Reference them as `/assets/icons/<name>.svg` on navigation, cards, and page `icon`
  fields. Mintlify's built-in chrome stays Lucide; only icons you set
  explicitly use this folder.
- Screenshots are lossy WebP at quality 90, captured from `https://diamond.shootstack.com` at desktop width
  in both light and dark appearance, cropped to the relevant panel, with the
  target control visible. Keep them under roughly 2500 px wide.
- File name encodes where it is used: `<article>-<task>-<n>.webp` for light and
  `<article>-<task>-<n>-dark.webp` for dark, so a rename of the article renames
  both images.
- Reference both from MDX inside one `<Frame>`. The light image uses
  `className="block dark:hidden"`. The dark image uses
  `className="hidden dark:block"` and the same `alt` text. See `help-mdx-copy.mdc`.
- Replacing a screenshot keeps the same filenames so no MDX changes.

## Boundaries

- No images embedded from external CDNs in articles.
- No screenshots containing real client names, emails, or photos. Use demo
  workspace data. Any email address a reader can see is `demo@shootstack.com`,
  not a personal address and not another invented address such as
  `jessica@shootstack.com` or `noura@shootstack.com`. Other demo contacts
  already named `demo+…@shootstack.com` may stay when a list needs more than
  one row. If a stored record still has a different address, rewrite that
  response for the capture. Do not save the rewrite back to the workspace.
- Do not add a top-level `icons/` or `images/` folder. Both live under `assets/`.
- `.gitignore` excludes stray root `dark.svg` / `light.svg`; logos belong
  under `assets/logo/`.
